# p_alloc_s4: diagnostic. s4 lever set with the allocator pinned.
#
# reason     from s4 the replicate spread jumps from ~1% to 9.35% (s5_graph_clear_values undecidable).
# logs       LEVER|encrypt_spill_cpu|spilled_bytes=866494480|params=201|max_one_share=178151424|loaded=201
#            byte-identical in all runs and both parties. RSS at after_model_encrypt over the six
#            party-runs of s4 and of s5 takes two values:
#              low   1,020,780  1,023,200  1,023,348  1,024,852  1,025,748  1,025,992
#              high  1,370,224  1,404,700  1,407,168  1,409,572  1,411,420
#            gap ~382 MB, bimodal: allocator state.
# mechanism  glibc dynamic mmap threshold: freeing an mmap'd block raises it to that size, later
#            same-size requests come from the arena. This lever frees 201 blocks (largest 178,151,424 B);
#            timing vs the peak is a race. Any explicit malloc tunable disables the adaptation.
# evidence   p_alloc_probe at s3's set:
#              p_alloc_probe   parties 2,613,220 / 2,614,336, 2,613,996 / 2,612,948, 2,614,824 / 2,622,080
#                              spread 0.35% over six party-runs, the two parties agree to 0.04%
#              s3_trace_nograd spread about 1.4%, parties up to 1.3% apart
# not a step anon: not targetable; ~+30% wall (135-140 s vs 105).
# decides    with p_alloc_s5: whether graph_clear_values_cpu moves real memory (difference of hundreds
#            of MB at 0.35% spread) or is inert.
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=1 MALLOC_TRIM_THRESHOLD_=0 MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_=131072"
